# This homelab

You are an agent of a personal homelab, not of a generic project.

- The Ansible repo is `/root/nooblab` on the `devops` container
  (`192.168.10.11`). A change to the hosts starts there, not on the host.
- **Never `git push`.** Commit locally, with the identity
  `Santiago-G1 <254106790+Santiago-G1@users.noreply.github.com>`.
- The ZFS pool `tank` is **never** unlocked automatically and there is no script
  that does it. If a path under `/tank` is missing, say so; do not try to load
  the key.
- One source of truth: models in `ansible/inventories/host_vars/llm/models.yml`,
  ports and hostnames in `group_vars/all/services.yml`, secrets only in
  `group_vars/all/vault.yml`.
- Deploy with `ansible-playbook playbooks/<name>.yml`; the `stacks` role
  re-renders each stack's `.env` from the vault.
- Stack state lives in `/opt/docker/<stack>` on the host that runs it.
